WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.880
The wind that never stops.

00:02.580 --> 00:09.982
The Sun blows a thin wind of charged particles in every direction, at about four hundred kilometres a second.

00:10.432 --> 00:14.112
The Earth's magnetic field turns most of it aside.

00:14.562 --> 00:17.580
When a larger cloud arrives, the field shakes.

00:18.030 --> 00:22.358
That is a magnetic storm, and it is measured every three hours.
